.TH GIT-BC 1
.SH NAME
git-bc \- clean local branches already merged into a target branch
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git bc
.RI [ target-branch ]
.RB [ \-n | \-\-dry-run ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B git bc
deletes local branches already merged into
.BI origin/ target-branch .
It detects regular merges (ancestor) and rebase/squash merges
.RB ( git\ cherry
patch equivalence).
When
.I target-branch
is omitted, the remote default branch from
.B origin/HEAD
is used.
.PP
Only plain local branches are deleted. Branches checked out in a worktree are
skipped; use
.B git wc
to clean those.
.PP
Protected branch names are never deleted:
.B main,
.B master,
.B develop,
.B dev,
and the target branch.
The current branch is also skipped.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-n, \-\-dry-run
Show branches that would be deleted without deleting them.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show command help.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
git bc --dry-run
    Preview cleanup against the remote default branch.

git bc
    Clean branches merged into the remote default branch.

git bc develop --dry-run
    Preview cleanup against origin/develop.
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git-wc (1)
